        <h1 class="post-detail__title">Community Counts: Blake Chapman Young Eagles Scholarship</h1>

        <div class="post-detail__featured-image">
          <img src="/assets/images/news/50000.webp" alt="Community Counts: Blake Chapman Young Eagles Scholarship" loading="lazy">
        </div>

        <div class="post-detail__content">
          <p>The <a href="https://cftetonvalley.org/blake-chapman-young-eagles-scholarship/">Blake Chapman Young Eagles Scholarship</a> allows the local Chapter 1049 of the Experimental Aircraft Association to provide funding for a high school junior or senior from Teton Valley, Idaho to earn their Private Pilot Certificate.&nbsp;&nbsp;This amazing opportunity can not only set them up on an incredible career path but also allow them to develop a sense of self-confidence and maturity that will carry them far in life.</p>

<p>The flight training is conducted at our local flight school, Teton Aviation at the Driggs Airport.&nbsp;&nbsp;The student begins with both one-on-one and small group instruction in the classroom and then in the airplane.&nbsp;&nbsp;Their first major milestone in training is their first solo flight. This becomes a defining moment in every pilot’s life.&nbsp;&nbsp;Their instructor will step out of the plane and the student becomes the pilot in command as they taxi out for their first take-off and landing all by themselves.&nbsp;&nbsp;It is an incredible feeling and achievement that our scholarship winners are very fortunate to experience.</p>

<p>Throughout the summer months, the student will continue mastering the skills and knowledge required to safely and proficiently fly the airplane and make all the decisions required to operate safely.&nbsp;&nbsp;The process culminates with a final test called a check-ride.&nbsp;&nbsp;This is a test with an examiner that requires them to demonstrate their knowledge and skills through both an oral exam and a flight test.&nbsp;&nbsp;The process can be quite stressful and possibly the hardest test they will take in their lifetime but learning to manage that stress and perform to their full potential is a very valuable achievement.</p>

<p>The experience comes full circle when students pass their check-ride and can then use their new privileges to take excited family and friends on flights, which proves that the journey was well worth the effort and challenge.&nbsp;&nbsp;The lessons that they learn not just about flying a plane but how to manage workload, time, stress, and decision making will carry them far in life.&nbsp;&nbsp;The self-esteem, confidence, and sense of achievement they develop will last a lifetime.</p>

<p>Any contributions the community can make to the Blake Chapman Young Eagles Scholarship will help set these lucky scholarship recipients up on a path to success in the skies and beyond.</p>

